 She was slowly checking the things in her lap when her mother returned, carrying a pot of yeast to place beside the open fireplace, where a gentle fire was burning on this cool May morning. She set a small tin plate on top of the pot, kissed the precious little baby, and then went out again. Baby Lila was used to being left alone, though she could always hear her mother. At those times she would sit among the pillows, toss her trinkets around, and proudly sing to herself. Sometimes she would flop onto a pillow and fall asleep.

