 One day Fred found an old saddle in the stable. He asked his friend Bertie to help him put it on a horse named Buttercup, so they could ride together. They fastened the saddle onto Buttercup's smooth back, and Freddie laughed, "Now we have a circus ride!" They brought a chair from the house and set it beside a cow named Miss Cow, who looked at them with big round eyes. The boys sat on the chair. Fred said, "I will count, and when I say four, we will jump onto the saddle." "One, two, three, four," he counted, and they leapt. But before they could say five, Buttercup's heels were in the air and her head fell quickly. Fred felt a sudden chill and found himself standing in a puddle of rainwater under the wood shed. Bertie, on the other hand, splashed into a pan of meal and water.

