 Una nodded a lot and they walked from the dark tunnels toward a small dam that turns a brook into a mill stream. The banks were low and bare, and the bright afternoon sun on the Long Pool below the dam made your eyes hurt.

When they stepped outside, they were amazed. A big grey horse was drinking at the pool, and the water around its mouth looked like melted gold. On the horse’s back sat an old, white-haired man in a loose shiny chainmail robe. He had no head covering, but a small iron helmet was hanging at his saddle. His reins were red leather, a few inches long, and his saddle had red straps that were held back and forward.

‘Look!’ said Una, as if Dan wasn’t watching. ‘It’s like the picture in your room—“Sir Isumbras at the Ford”.’

