Let’s talk about tau protein. Tau helps build the long, thin parts of neurons called axons. These axons let neurons talk to each other. When tau builds up, it stops neurons from talking properly. That can cause confusion, bad thoughts, and changes in how people act. It can also cause memory problems, slow movement, and loss of thinking ability.

