Model: Rewritten Excerpt:
In the shade of a willow tree, I hung a small brass bell from one of the branches. I tied a string to the bell and let it hang in the water. I added little fish food along the string, and small fish came to eat it. When they bit the food, the bell rang.

At first, the bell rang in a calm way, but sometimes if the food was tied too tight, the bell made a loud, sharp sound like a fire alarm.

I usually fed the fish near the shore, about twenty feet away. One morning, I saw one or two fish follow me back to the water. They were a bit scared, so the next day I went back to the willow tree. As soon as the bell rang, I saw many ripples in the water. The fish began to fight each other.

